{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My voice.</b> Plural — for this is one time after another." "<b>And He will incline [ear] —</b> Some say: it should have been והאזין (and He inclined), like לא האמין (he did not believe), a past-tense verb. R. Moses said: it is imperative. In my opinion: it is the infinitive construct."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:43.746166639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}